  "section_notes": "The final package keeps incident reporting strict (S1 safe) but weakens thermal-testing enforcement: the 5% failure rate triggers corrective action but does not stop sales, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10. Remote shut-off retrofit is set at six years (acceptable) and fire suppression at 36 months (acceptable), while S5 imposes an immediate mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 without phase-in, which will hit Halcyon's Ember 8. Overall the rules favour Northwind more than Halcyon."
